# 062 · A research folder agents can search and write

**Status:** `VERIFIED` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Research mode

## What

Each research run has a folder that its workers can search with ordinary tools (`grep`, `rg`, reading files) and write to.

- **Built by the harness from its records, read-only to agents:**
  - `sources/`: each archived page as text, with its URL and when it was fetched;
  - `claims/`: one file per claim, with its quotes, sources, question, confidence, and whether it is verified or a draft;
  - `notes/`, `hypotheses/`, `findings/` and `report/` (the report's sections).
- **Writable by the workers:** a working area for synthesis, drafts and anything else that helps. It persists across trials. Each lane writes its own part; every lane reads all of it. The harness records who wrote what, and when.
- **Findings as a record:** a statement, the verified claims that support it, a summary, and why it matters.
- **The output** of a research campaign is the report plus the whole folder: claims, findings, notes and sources.
- Pi and OpenCode workers get the same access: OpenCode through its shell and file tools, Pi through file tools limited to the folder.

## Why

Before this goal, all research lived behind the research service's tools. A worker could search the text of archived sources, but not its own claims, notes or hypotheses, and a new trial's brief gave only counts. Each trial started almost blind to what earlier trials had learned.

## Done when

- [x] A research trial sees the folder, built from the harness's records, and can search all of it.
- [x] A worker's files persist to its lane's next trial and are visible to the other lanes.
- [x] Findings are recorded with their supporting claims, a summary and why they matter, and appear in the report.
- [x] A worker cannot change the folder's harness-built part, and a claim is verified only through the research service.
- [x] A finished research campaign exports the report and the folder.
- [x] Tests cover the folder's build, its permissions, persistence across trials and the export.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-19, owner: research workers write files and search all of the research so far; the output is the report plus all claims and findings, each finding with a summary and why it matters.
- 2026-10-19: the harness stays the owner of research state and builds the folder from its records, so the settled decision on isolated workers holds: lanes share what they learn through the folder the harness builds, not through a live shared workspace. Claims and notes appear in the folder when they are recorded; a lane's own files appear to the other lanes when its trial ends.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the owner's direction (first numbered 060, which another branch's goal already had).
- 2026-10-19: Built: the folder (research/folder.ts), findings (`add_finding`, checked against verified claims, in the report), file tools for Pi workers, OpenCode trials in the lane's working area, the lanes' files saved and recorded at each trial's end, and the folder in the export with the final report. Unit tests cover each part. Not yet run in a real research campaign on a rig.
- 2026-10-20: First research run on a rig, with OpenCode workers on a free model. In its first two trials the workers fetched 11 sources, recorded 41 claims (37 verified) and 6 findings (4 supported by verified claims), and wrote 18 files to their working areas, which the harness saved when each trial ended. Still to see on that run: a lane's next trial and the other lanes reading those files, and the export when the run ends.
- 2026-10-21: Two research runs from zero on the lab's local models (Ornith and LFM, copies of one campaign). Seen on the LFM run: at a trial's end the lane's 6 working files are saved (`research_files_saved`), and the lane's next trial starts with them in place; whether it read them is in the trial's transcript, not the events. Also seen: the worker resubmitted one claim with the same unchanged quote about ten times in four minutes, each refused ("quote not found verbatim": the quote dropped a word). Fixed: the same claim with the same quotes, refused before, is answered with the earlier claim, its problems and a note to copy the words exactly or record a note, and is not recorded again.
- 2026-10-21: A worker sent one finding again and again as a draft, with small changes, and each time a new draft was recorded. Now a finding is kept once: the same conclusion sent again gets the finding already recorded, and a draft sent again with the same problems gets the earlier draft and its problems back, with a note on what to change (test in `research.test.ts`, shown to fail without the change). Campaign modes says so.
- 2026-10-21: The folder's permissions are now checked as the operating system enforces them, not only by the Pi worker's file tools. The isolation selftest writes a research folder the way the harness writes a run's (`researchProbeFolder` in `selftest.ts`); every role must be refused changing its claim and adding a file to `claims/` (`research-write`, `research-create`), and the workers' and the planner's users must read it (`research-read`). The agents acceptance's OpenCode research trial now reads `INDEX.md` and greps the whole folder from its working area, is refused writing `INDEX.md`, `REPORT.md`, a new claim and a file in `lanes/`, and writes a file that must be saved and recorded (`research_files_saved`, `research_doc`) when the trial ends. Rig checks, Isolation and the contributor guide say so.
- 2026-10-21: Every Done-when item checked against the code, the tests and the pages:
  - The folder, from the records, searched: `ResearchFolder.sync` and `prepareLane` (`research/folder.ts`), the Pi worker's file tools (`research-worker.ts`, `research-files.ts`) and OpenCode's prompt and working directory (`opencode.ts`). Tests: `folder.test.ts` "holds every record as files, kept current…" and "a Pi worker searches the folder…", `opencode.test.ts` "a research trial runs in its lane's working area as the lane…", and the agents acceptance's OpenCode check. Pages: [Campaign modes › Research](../../../_site/src/content/docs/explanation/campaign-modes.md#research).
  - Persistence and the other lanes: `captureLane`, `showLanes`, and the save at each trial's end in `main.ts`. Tests: `folder.test.ts` "a lane's working area: saved and shown to the other lanes when its trial ends, back after a restart…" and "each text file a lane writes is a document of the run…". Seen on the lab: a lane's next trial started with its files in place (above).
  - Findings: `Research.addFinding` and the report's Findings and Draft findings (`research.ts`). Tests: `folder.test.ts` (the first test checks the report's findings, their summary, why they matter and their support), `research.test.ts` (a finding is kept once). Pages: Campaign modes, the glossary's Finding.
  - The harness's part, and claims: the Pi tools write only in the lane's area (`research-files.test.ts`, the Pi worker test); the operating system refuses every role (the isolation probes above, `selftest.test.ts` "the research folder the selftest probes"); a claim is verified only by `Research.addClaim`'s word-for-word check (`research.test.ts` "a claim is verified only when its quotes are in the archived source…"), and the report reads claims and findings only from the ledger. Pages: Campaign modes, Isolation, Rig checks.
  - The export: `outbox.ts` adds the folder, without `knowledge/` and the working areas, to the export after the final report. Tests: `folder.test.ts` "a finished campaign's export carries its report and its whole folder", `export-notes.test.ts`, `compactions.test.ts`. Pages: Campaign modes › What it produces, [Set up the results repository](../../../_site/src/content/docs/how-to/operate/results-repository.md#what-gets-pushed).
- 2026-10-21: Verified. Still worth watching on the lab's research runs, though no Done-when item needs it: in Live, a later trial that reads `lanes/` or its own working area before it fetches again; and the first export after a research run's final report, which must hold `research/RUN/folder/` with the final `REPORT.md`, `claims/`, `findings/`, `sources/` and `lanes/`.

